<title>JAPAN: EIB launches 30 bln yen 5.6% yen/A$ samurai.</title>
<headline>EIB launches 30 bln yen 5.6% yen/A$ samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Yamaichi Securities on Tuesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  European Investment Bank (EIB)</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.6 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  31 May 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  30 May 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	May 13 to May 29</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Yamaichi Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,048.47 per 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
